                        ],
                        "form": "вороже́ями"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "06ac45e2-878b-4e8f-bb60-8c3992ea592d",
                        "entry_id": "dc3b72d4-7adc-38c8-9e90-351231f282c8",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "вороже́е"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "592edc03-c0e0-4eac-b635-edec346bb473",
                        "entry_id": "dc3b72d4-7adc-38c8-9e90-351231f282c8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "вороже́ях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "baa3f8da-d38f-3d65-b87b-ffec41de9bfa",
                        "entry_id": "dc3b72d4-7adc-38c8-9e90-351231f282c8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "женск. к ворожей; женщина, занимающаяся ворожбой; колдунья; гадалка"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bf48041-e3ad-4cce-ae35-645630dcfd9c",
                                "sense_id": "baa3f8da-d38f-3d65-b87b-ffec41de9bfa",
                                "text": "«Я позову старуху, ворожею; против её никакая сила не устоит. Она выльет переполох тебе»."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c12442d6-bbe5-45cd-a5bd-0f30cc6348c0",
                                "sense_id": "baa3f8da-d38f-3d65-b87b-ffec41de9bfa",
                                "text": "Ревнивые мужья хотели от ворожей узнавать о неверности своих жён. Ворожею призывали в дом: она присматривалась к сердцу женщины, которую муж подвергал испытанию; если ворожея замечала, что у жены сердце трепещет, то укоряла её в неверности и отдавала невинную на произвольную расправу мужа."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2adc0ad-2dd3-4c3b-8fb7-f9197ae7bf70",
                                "sense_id": "baa3f8da-d38f-3d65-b87b-ffec41de9bfa",
                                "text": "Но живёт в Куйбышеве одна старушка — тайная ворожея и лечит заговором, берёт по десятке."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a672478a-bdd3-4dca-9ae6-86de7435f1c1",
                        "source_entry_id": "dc3b72d4-7adc-38c8-9e90-351231f282c8",
                        "source_sense_id": "baa3f8da-d38f-3d65-b87b-ffec41de9bfa",
                        "target_lang_word": "fortune-teller",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fortune-teller",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9847f24a-f947-3452-a54e-32069c075f73",
                                        "entry_id": "c8e09518-ff9b-334c-8125-5f26054a218a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who professes to predict the future in return for money."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b104375-e7a8-4db6-87fb-b50c83e2df5c",
                                                "sense_id": "9847f24a-f947-3452-a54e-32069c075f73",
                                                "text": "\"Cross my palm with silver and I'll tell you your fortune,\" said the fortune-teller."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "034ad2d7-8dfe-4a49-a068-3c901f36b5d2",
                                                "sense_id": "9847f24a-f947-3452-a54e-32069c075f73",
                                                "text": "So I guess the fortune teller's right / I should've seen just what was there"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "835f6212-a660-3069-a0bf-436ba42cd649",
                                        "entry_id": "c8e09518-ff9b-334c-8125-5f26054a218a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cootie catcher."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5040ae2-533a-4c2a-8d94-f879e517bb9c",
                                                "sense_id": "835f6212-a660-3069-a0bf-436ba42cd649",
                                                "text": "The usual exchange between English children is as follows: A: Who do you love? (referring to one of the names on the fortune-teller) B: Simon. A: S-I-M-O-N (alternately opens and shuts the device as he or she says each letter)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f82a3e69-c53c-4fe8-a317-f099feaa2b8d",
                        "source_entry_id": "dc3b72d4-7adc-38c8-9e90-351231f282c8",
                        "source_sense_id": "baa3f8da-d38f-3d65-b87b-ffec41de9bfa",
                        "target_lang_word": "seer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "seer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "931705a2-ef31-3eb2-b854-841f789e4d9e",
                                        "entry_id": "56a15d9b-c8d2-3989-a8a0-47ea59bde15d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who foretells the future; a clairvoyant, prophet, soothsayer or diviner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15bcadb6-3246-42c9-9b7c-5d10a0733501",
                                                "sense_id": "931705a2-ef31-3eb2-b854-841f789e4d9e",
                                                "text": "\"But I must not forget to tell you that the lad was born on a Sunday, and had found a card with the four of clubs; therefore he was a seer, that is to say, he could see the supernatural people, but they could not see him.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a019784-6834-34c7-af97-0f87d605a95b",
                                        "entry_id": "56a15d9b-c8d2-3989-a8a0-47ea59bde15d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who sees something; an eyewitness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68bd5688-141b-496d-894d-e3b75e8be0db",
                                                "sense_id": "1a019784-6834-34c7-af97-0f87d605a95b",
                                                "text": "As a seer of beautiful visions, or, shall we say, of visions of the beautiful, he is never weary of celebrating the poet and his vocation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "seer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
